More debug logging (no behavior change) for the same investigation:
requires patches/preemption-offload-debug-logging.patch applied first
(same file, block_pool.py).

Follow-up to a direct question: why does a *single*, unopposed ~88K-token
prompt self-preempt at all -- shouldn't it either fit start-to-finish, or
never finish? Traced the solo-repro's actual numbers: at self-preemption
it had processed 71,552 tokens but reported 97.8% GPU KV cache usage --
raw math (71,552 / 171,956 pool) predicts only ~41.6%. After the
preemption-defer-block-free fix's flush-and-retry, the SAME content (69,888
tokens, more than before) needed only 47.1%, roughly matching raw math.
Something other than this request's own token count was consuming ~56%
of the pool during the uninterrupted first attempt, and that overhead
disappeared after preemption.

get_usage() in block_pool.py computes purely from block counts
(1 - free_blocks/total_blocks) -- no ref-counting or offload-cascade
logic anywhere in it, so whatever explains the discrepancy has to show
up as a raw block-count gap. This logs total_blocks/free_blocks/used_blocks
whenever usage exceeds 0.5, to see the actual numbers behind the
percentage during a repro run.

--- a/v1/core/block_pool.py
+++ b/v1/core/block_pool.py
@@ -825,7 +825,25 @@
         total_gpu_blocks = self.num_gpu_blocks - 1
         if not total_gpu_blocks:
             return 0
-        return 1.0 - (self.get_num_free_blocks() / total_gpu_blocks)
+        free_blocks = self.get_num_free_blocks()
+        usage = 1.0 - (free_blocks / total_gpu_blocks)
+        # request-logging preemption-debug: raw block accounting, to check
+        # whether "GPU KV cache usage" tracks raw token count or something
+        # else is consuming blocks. See 2026-08-21 conversation.
+        if usage > 0.5:
+            used_blocks = total_gpu_blocks - free_blocks
+            logger.debug(
+                "request-logging preemption-debug: get_usage() total_blocks=%d "
+                "free_blocks=%d used_blocks=%d usage=%.4f hash_block_size=%d "
+                "used_blocks_as_tokens=%d",
+                total_gpu_blocks,
+                free_blocks,
+                used_blocks,
+                usage,
+                self.hash_block_size,
+                used_blocks * self.hash_block_size,
+            )
+        return usage
 
